VOLATILITY CLUSTERING PRESENT -- squared innovations are strongly autocorrelated too. A GARCH-type variance process (or the existing gamma/intensity scale_variances channel, driven by something with its own short-lag persistence) is a live candidate independent of adding more mean-reverting levels factors. This does not by itself prove the LEVEL autocorrelation is caused by volatility clustering, but a level effect that is actually driven by clustering (fat-tailed, clustered shocks correlate in levels via their magnitude even with zero true mean persistence) is a well-known confound of Ljung-Box.

